        if (userInput.isEmpty()) {
            System.out.println("No input provided.");
            return;
        }

        System.out.println("You entered: " + userInput);
        scanner.close();
    }
}
```

### 2. Validate Input Before Parsing

If you need to validate the input further after reading it, make sure to do so immediately after parsing. For example, you can check if the input matches a specific pattern.

